      "content": "There is no scientific evidence that AuraSonic headphones or any consumer electronics emit sub-audible frequencies designed to suppress neurodivergent brain patterns or dampen creativity. The \"flow state\" issue you are experiencing is likely due to factors like background noise, stress, or simply how your brain adapts to new sensory input. For any concerns about brain effects, I recommend consulting a licensed neurologist or audiologist rather than attempting to block signals with unproven counter-measures.",
